BUGS FIXED:

1. EMAIL DELIMITER BUG (BUG 1)
   Problem: Script used space delimiter (cut -d' ') for emails.dat which is tab-delimited
   Impact: Emails were not parsed correctly, causing field misalignment
   Fix: Changed to use tab delimiter: awk -F$'\t' when parsing emails.dat

2. SORTING MISMATCH BUG (BUG 2)  
   Problem: Users sorted alphabetically by username, emails sorted numerically by UID
            Then pasted together line-by-line causing complete misalignment
   Impact: Wrong emails matched to wrong users
   Fix: Removed sorting/pasting logic; now directly reads users.dat and looks up
        emails by UID using awk, ensuring correct UID-based joins

3. GROUP DELIMITER BUG (BUG 3)
   Problem: groups.dat is colon-delimited but awk used default space/tab separator
   Impact: Group names not resolved, GIDs appeared in output instead of names
   Fix: Added -F: to all awk commands when parsing groups.dat

VERIFICATION:
- Tested with user 'aadams' (UID 1482)
- All fields correctly aligned: username, UID, primary group, email, shell, supplementary groups
- Group names properly resolved (engineering, analytics, database)
- All 800 users exported successfully

